yasb.log

# Claude Code
# The root .claude/ is mostly Claude Code's own state (sessions, history,
# backups, file-history, plugins, shell snapshots), so its contents are ignored
# by default. .claude/skills/ is the exception: cloud sessions clone this
# repository and read project skills from there, and they never see
# ~/.claude/skills on any machine.
#
# It has to be written as `/.claude/*` rather than `/.claude/`: git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a negation for something inside one is
# silently ignored. Excluding the entries instead leaves the directory itself
# readable, which is what makes the next line work.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/history.jsonl
**/.claude/sessions/
**/.claude/session-env/
**/.claude/file-history/
**/.claude/shell-snapshots/
**/.claude/backups/
**/.claude/cache/
**/.claude/projects/
**/.claude/.last-cleanup
